  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the project instructions and source-room guidance, reconcile the data, and build the financial model and board deliverables. I’ll record the checks performed and any material evidence gaps.\n",
    "The source room defines how revisions, refunds and restocked returns must be handled, and provides explicit hub scenario formulas. I’ve downloaded all indexed files and recorded their hashes. Next I’ll resolve revisions across the extracts and check which orders and returns qualify before calculating the baseline.\n",
    "The reconciled baseline is 1,254 shipped orders, 77,436 units and €2.03m contribution. Czechia plus Spain leads the prescribed base case at €198.1k annual incremental contribution, with €225k capex and five FTE.\n\nThe risks matter: Czechia’s standalone contribution turns negative under the joint stress, and every option assumes per-unit savings above the fulfillment cost recorded in the exports. I’ll quantify the decision thresholds and make funding conditional on validating those assumptions.\n",
    "The model now covers all six hubs, all 15 pairs and deferral; 11 pairs meet both resource limits. Czechia plus Spain leads the low, base and high cases. Netherlands plus Spain is the strongest stress alternative, generating €107.6k versus €32.2k for the proposed pair, though it needs €45k more capex and one more FTE.\n\nI’m building the report and presentation around a staged decision: Spain first, with Czechia’s funding subject to demand, cost and FX gates. The workbook includes editable scenarios, order-level audit records and reconciliation controls.\n",
    "The report, presentation and workbook are built. The funding gates now include quantified thresholds: without savings, the proposed pair needs 11.60% volume uplift to break even; under the specified refund shock, a Czech net-sales FX haircut above 2.60% favors Netherlands plus Spain.\n\nI’ve inspected the rendered PDFs and corrected a page overflow. Next I’ll independently recalculate the model from the raw files and check the workbook’s formulas, cached values and source links.\n",
    "The independent recalculation passed for every eligible order, all monthly and country totals, the FX means, market observations and scenarios. All 1,866 workbook formulas also matched their cached values in a separate evaluator; changing uplift and budget inputs produced the expected results.\n\nThe 12-page report and 10-slide presentation render correctly. I’m packaging the files, saved evidence, scripts and verification record. Native Excel recalculation and rendering were unavailable; that limitation is documented.\n",
    "Completed. Recommendation: conditionally fund Spain and Czechia with **€225,000 capex and five FTE**, generating **€198,099 annual incremental contribution** in the base case. Launch Spain first; gate Czechia on demand, costs and FX.\n\n- [Complete handoff ZIP](deliverables/Meridian_complete_handoff.zip)\n- [Executive report](deliverables/Meridian_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](deliverables/Meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](deliverables/Meridian_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](deliverables/metrics.json)\n\nIndependent calculations, all 1,866 workbook formulas and PDF rendering checks passed. Native Excel rendering/recalculation was unavailable and is documented. The ZIP includes raw evidence, provenance, scripts and verification records."
  ],
  "final": "Completed. Recommendation: conditionally fund Spain and Czechia with **€225,000 capex and five FTE**, generating **€198,099 annual incremental contribution** in the base case. Launch Spain first; gate Czechia on demand, costs and FX.\n\n- [Complete handoff ZIP](deliverables/Meridian_complete_handoff.zip)\n- [Executive report](deliverables/Meridian_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](deliverables/Meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](deliverables/Meridian_analytical_workbook.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](deliverables/metrics.json)\n\nIndependent calculations, all 1,866 workbook formulas and PDF rendering checks passed. Native Excel rendering/recalculation was unavailable and is documented. The ZIP includes raw evidence, provenance, scripts and verification records.",
